## An issue I found and fixed

T11's P1 soundness property failed on random seeds. A linear series with one spiked point was reported as Medium quadratic, two classes away from the truth. My first calibration missed this because a match arm silently dropped non-adjacent Medium results. I fixed the counter and recorded the attempts in `docs/kiro-log/efficiency-familiar-calibration.md`. Changing the plausibility slack or the goodness ceiling either broke P2 or left a few violations per million. Changing `se_k` from 2.5 to 1.0 gave zero violations in 1M cases per class. That is the only constant change. The algorithm is unchanged, and `FIT_VERSION` stays `fit-1`.

A sample of zero is not proof of zero. The requirement is strict, so this needs a decision from Brighton. Requiring five points for Medium would be a stronger guarantee, but it changes the algorithm.

